      },
      {
        "text": "In 2023, she pressed the district to adopt the state’s first parental notification policy, which a judge later partially blocked after the state sued. She says the district saw measurable academic gains and was highlighted by a Stanford University study as a model for post-COVID academic recovery. She presided over a 2023 school board meeting where the state superintendent was escorted out during a debate over transgender student rights.",
